    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW25KWiJPRkGcgDQT8pc4YUMR)_\n\nFollows #354 (merged).\n\n## What\n- `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-order` and `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-indent` no longer work in batches of 50 with apply/skip per batch. They apply to the whole file at once:\n  - one yes-or-no question that says how many entries it will fix\n  - the file is copied to `sp-bibtex-lint-backup-directory` before it is written\n  - still refuses when the open buffer is unsaved or the file changed on disk since the lint\n  - entries with a comment inside are still left alone\n- Author names (`sp-bibtex-lint-fix-authors`) keep the batches of `sp-bibtex-lint-batch-size` (50) with their choices.\n- The report and the literate doc (bullet lists) say which fixes are whole-file and which are batched.\n\n## Tests\n- 42 tests (this file and `sp-batch-report`) pass in Emacs 29 with `sp-cache-dir` and `sp-var-dir` defined. New or changed: order applied in one question for 5 entries with a batch size of 2, declining writes nothing and makes no backup, batches now tested through the author names, file-changed-on-disk through the single question.\n- Not run on the real `.bib` files or in Emacs 31.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edits, per the nightly-tidy rule. The branch is not prefixed with the PR number, because the session's branch name was fixed.\n\n---\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCsguMS2m92TG5VLGt)_",
